{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) has assigned task #5246: implement `cmd/echo` for the go-unix-utils project, specifically covering srd020-echo requirements R1.1 through R1.4 (core output behavior). The task requires creating two files: `cmd/echo/main.go` (implementation) and `cmd/echo/echo_test.go` (differential tests against gecho). The implementation must match GNU echo (gecho) byte-for-byte behavior, follow project coding standards, pass compilation, vet, and tests.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - **GNU echo flag parsing**: Echo does NOT use standard getopt. Flags are only recognized if an argument consists entirely of `-` followed by combinations of `n`, `e`, `E`. Once a non-flag argument appears, everything is literal.\n   - **Differential testing pattern**: Tests compare Go binary output against Homebrew GNU reference binary (gecho) using `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - **SIGPIPE handling**: All cmd/ utilities must call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` at start of main\n   - **Copyright header**: Every Go file must start with SPDX copyright header\n   - **No git commands**: Git is managed externally by the orchestrator\n   - **Write-first strategy**: Write all source files before running any build/test commands\n   - **LC_ALL=C**: Test environment uses C locale for consistent behavior\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd020-echo.yaml`** (READ - provides exact specification):\n     - R1.1: Write arguments to stdout, separated by spaces, followed by newline\n     - R1.2: No arguments → write only a newline\n     - R1.3: `-n` suppresses trailing newline\n     - R1.4: Unrecognized flags starting with \"-\" are literal text; recognized flags are `-n`, `-e`, `-E`\n     - R2.1-R2.4: Escape sequences (-e/-E) - NOT in this task's scope but flags must be recognized\n     - R3.1-R3.3: Exit codes (0 success, 1 write error) and SIGPIPE handling\n     - R4.1-R4.3: Differential testing requirements\n     - Non-goals: No --help/--version, no XSI-compliant behavior, no stdin reading\n   \n   - **`pkg/sys/sigpipe.go`** (provided in project_context - pattern to follow):\n     ```go\n     func InstallSIGPIPEHandler() {\n         c := make(chan os.Signal, 1)\n         signal.Notify(c, syscall.SIGPIPE)\n         go func() {\n             <-c\n             os.Exit(0)\n         }()\n     }\n     ```\n   \n   - **`pkg/testutils/difftest.go`** (provided in project_context - DiffTest struct and RunDiffTests signature):\n     ```go\n     type DiffTest struct {\n         Name          string\n         Args          []string\n         Stdin         []byte\n         Env           []string\n         WorkDir       string\n         ExitCode      int\n         Normalize     []NormalizeFunc\n         ExpectedFiles map[string][]byte\n     }\n     func RunDiffTests(t *testing.T, goBinary, refBinary string, tests []DiffTest)\n     ```\n   \n   - **`cmd/echo/main.go`** - TO BE CREATED: echo implementation\n   - **`cmd/echo/echo_test.go`** - TO BE CREATED: differential tests\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Only one tool call (Read) was made successfully before the summary request.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Read the SRD to understand the full echo specification\n   - Identified that R1.1-R1.4 are the core output requirements in scope\n   - Recognized that GNU echo has special flag parsing (not standard getopt): flags must be arguments consisting entirely of `-` plus any combination of `n`, `e`, `E` characters\n   - Determined that while `-e` and `-E` must be recognized as flags per R1.4, only `-n` needs functional implementation in this task (escape handling is R2.x, not in scope)\n   - Default behavior is `-E` (no escape interpretation), so recognizing `-e`/`-E` without escape implementation is correct behavior\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - Message 1: The complete task prompt from the cobbler orchestrator containing project context, SRDs, source code, execution constitution, coding standards, and task description for implementing cmd/echo R1.1-R1.4\n   - Message 2: \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools.\" - requesting a summary of conversation\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Create `cmd/echo/main.go` with implementation of R1.1-R1.4 (core output behavior, -n flag, flag recognition)\n   - Create `cmd/echo/echo_test.go` with differential tests against gecho\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/echo/` to verify no issues\n   - Run `go build -o bin/echo ./cmd/echo/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/echo/ -count=1` to verify tests pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading the SRD file (`docs/specs/software-requirements/srd020-echo.yaml`) to understand the exact specification for R1.1-R1.4. I was about to begin the implementation phase - writing both `cmd/echo/main.go` and `cmd/echo/echo_test.go` before running any build/test commands.\n\n   The implementation plan based on the SRD:\n   - `main.go`: Parse arguments manually (not with flag package) to match GNU echo's flag handling. Recognized flag arguments consist of `-` followed only by chars from set {n, e, E}. Track escapeMode and noNewline booleans. Join remaining args with spaces, write to stdout, optionally append newline. Call `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` first. Handle write errors with exit code 1.\n   - `echo_test.go`: Use `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")`, `exec.LookPath(\"gecho\")` with t.Skip, create DiffTest cases for: no args, single arg, multiple args, -n flag, unrecognized flags as literal text, combined flags like -nE, and arguments starting with \"-\" that aren't valid flags.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write both `cmd/echo/main.go` and `cmd/echo/echo_test.go` in their entirety, then r