{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01UUBQSXuytEUZ2h5butxydx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The `--help` and `--version` tests fail because gecho actually processes `--help` and `--version` as special flags, outputting help/version text. But the SRD non-goals say: \"cmd/echo does not implement --help or --version (GNU echo does not process these as flags either; they are printed as literals).\"\n\nWait, but the differential test shows gecho DOES handle --help and --version. The SRD is wrong about GNU echo not processing them? Let me think...\n\nActually, looking at the gecho output, it clearly processes `--help` and `--version`. \n\nThe SRD's claim about GNU echo is inaccurate for the Homebrew version we're testing against, but since the SRD explicitly marks these as non-goals for our implementation, I should just remove those test cases rather than try to match gecho's behavior.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2725,"cache_read_input_tokens":38266,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2725},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4803ee21-8ebf-4ff1-ae3b-2b34c42a3c29","uuid":"b53b8031-d86b-4f04-8c7a-599901154d3c"}
